3. postal-codes.json
--------------------

Contains the postal-code patterns ("zip") and examples ("zipex") of the address metadata of
Google's libaddressinput project (https://github.com/google/libaddressinput), commit
81eb9628382b07d371d8ea0b11badf7de3857fd5, testdata/countryinfo.txt. That data is licensed under
the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/); the project's README states: "Data licensed
under the CC-BY 4.0". Changes: only each country's pattern and examples are kept, and three
examples that contradict their own patterns are left out (BY 20050, EE 1001, GB RH6 OHP). The
data is provided as is, without warranties.


4. nicknames.json
-----------------

Pairs whose sources include "authored" are OpenVerify's own (Apache-2.0). Pairs whose sources
include "wikidata:<item>/<item>" were accepted by a reviewer from Wikidata
(https://www.wikidata.org); Wikidata's structured data is dedicated to the public domain under
CC0 1.0 (https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:Licensing), so no attribution is required. It is
credited here as a courtesy.
